claire-cs: Onboarding stuck for Nimbus. Mobile app (Android) rollout ~180 devices -> many 401 then 429 during SDK init.

dan-platform: SDK version and token type?

claire-cs: android-sdk 1.4.1, ephemeral tokens via their /auth/session endpoint. Logs: `POST /v1/generate 401` then `POST /v1/generate 429 rate_limit`. They call SDK.init from splash + background sync concurrently.

raj-eng: Likely token stampede + retry amplification. Quick remediation: serialize SDK.init (single guard), ensure token is awaited, add small randomized jitter (300-1200ms) after token before heavy calls, and use interceptor to add Authorization per-request. Also change retry-on-401 to refresh+single-replay with backoff.

anya-support: KB snippet for Android we can send:
```
// single init guard
if (initGuard.compareAndSet(false,true)) {
  executor.execute(() -> {
    String t = fetchTokenBlocking();
    Thread.sleep(randBetween(300,1200));
    RedwoodSdk.initWithToken(context, t);
    initGuard.set(false);
  });
}
// add header in OkHttp interceptor per request
```

dan-platform: Short-term server-side smoothing: have /auth/session return a cached token for 2-4s under detected bursts or gate issuance with a small semaphore.

notif-bot: [metric-alert] edge.rate.nimbus spike -> 429 +360% in 5m.

claire-cs: Customer applied single-init + 800ms jitter + reduced preflight concurrency. They confirm 429s dropped to baseline. I'll add a short onboarding note about mobile init patterns. Closing.
